# SG Couture web storefront

Standalone Next.js 16 App Router frontend for `sg-couture-api`. **No database and no backend of its own.**

- API contract: `docs/integration/storefront/` — vendored, **read-only**. Never edit it or invent endpoints or fields not documented there.
- Plan/status: `docs/README.md`. Architecture: `docs/00-architecture.md`. Conventions: `docs/01-conventions.md`.
- Replies: extremely concise. No fluff, no long code snippets.

## Engineering posture

Act as a senior Next.js developer. Prefer App Router, Server Components, Server Actions, `proxy.ts`, `revalidatePath`, and `server-only`. Never use client-side fetching, `useEffect` data loading, or client state for server data when an RSC/Server Action exists.

## Consult before coding

- Unfamiliar library/framework APIs → **`docs-explorer`** (project MCPs + Context7). Do not rely on training-data APIs.
- Architecture decision, convention/API deviation, or refactor touching 3+ files → **`fable-advisor`**. A **Flag** is blocking until you fix the plan or explain why it does not apply.
